# The Prisma control schema the staging rebuild may drop, identified by its marker
# (reset-staging-baseline.sh, #1781).
#
# What approving the line below does: the rebuild drops the whole `prisma_contract` schema, not one
# row. That is three tables and every row in each — `marker`, `ledger` (with its id sequence) and
# `contract` — which is everything a Prisma migration writes there. It drops them by name, in one
# transaction as `migrator`, the schema's owner, after the backup branch; `public` is rebuilt in a
# second transaction, as `neondb_owner`, and no transaction spans both. If the schema holds any
# other object, or anything outside it depends on one of the three, the drop fails and that
# transaction rolls back, leaving `public` untouched. No other schema is reachable from it,
# `neon_auth` included.
#
