# `prisma_contract.marker` holds, each written exactly as the refusal quotes it — the space and the
# updated_at instant to the microsecond. Another space, another instant, or a row this record does
# not name, refuses as though the record were absent. The ledger's and contract's rows are not
# enumerated here; they go because they belong to the marker named below. A line that is not
# exactly one marker row refuses the reset by name, so no pattern can approve a schema. A backup
# branch the rebuild would reuse that was taken before the schema's last write refuses.
